@startuml
title SaveEye Pi/server deployment (default ports)
top to bottom direction

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 250

node "SaveEye device\nWi-Fi / Local MQTT" as Device <<device>>

node "Raspberry Pi 5\n64-bit Raspberry Pi OS" as Pi {
  package "Docker Compose: saveeye-edge" {
    queue "Local Mosquitto\nPi LAN IP:1883" as LocalBroker
    component "SaveEyeEdgeListenerApp\nSpin + MQTT trigger\nARM64 container" as Edge
    artifact "mosquitto-data\npersistent volume" as LocalData
  }
}

node "Laptop / server" as Server {
  package "Docker Compose: pwrusagesensorbackend" {
    queue "Server Mosquitto\nserver LAN IP:1884\n127.0.0.1:1884" as ServerBroker
    artifact "sensor-mosquitto-data\npersistent volume" as ServerData
  }
  node "Native systemd service\nuser: pwrusage-sensor" {
    component "pwrusagesensorbackend\nSpin + MQTT trigger\n/opt/pwrusagesensorbackend" as Backend
  }
  package "Existing Docker service (not recreated)" {
    database "PostgreSQL 18 / postgres18\n127.0.0.1:5432\nsaveeye.latest_readings" as Db
  }
}

Device --> LocalBroker : publish saveeye/telemetry\naccount: saveeye-device
LocalBroker --> Edge : subscription / MQTT trigger, QoS 1\naccount: saveeye-listener
Edge --> ServerBroker : publish pwrusage/sensors/saveeye/v1\nLAN MQTT, QoS 1, non-retained\naccount: sensor-edge
ServerBroker --> Backend : subscription / MQTT trigger, QoS 1\nbackend connects over loopback\naccount: sensor-backend
Backend --> Db : parameterized upsert over loopback\nrole: saveeye_listener
LocalBroker ..> LocalData : broker state
ServerBroker ..> ServerData : broker state

note bottom of Edge
Source: iotdevices/SaveEyeEdgeListenerApp
Runs composed.wasm with telemetry processor.
Validates, filters, normalizes, envelopes.
No database credentials or capability.
Outbound publish deadline: 5 seconds.
end note

note bottom of Backend
Source: pwerusage/pwrusagesensorbackend
Runs composed.wasm with telemetry processor.
Validates envelope; owns database access.
Latest per device serial; newer edge timestamp wins.
edge_id and backend_received_at retain provenance.
end note

note top of ServerBroker
Envelope: schemaVersion = 1, edgeId, reading.
reading.receivedAt is the Pi receipt timestamp.
Publisher credentials authenticate the account,
not a cryptographic binding of edgeId.
end note

legend bottom
  Trusted LAN only: authenticated MQTT is not encrypted.
  PostgreSQL stays loopback-only; no Pi-to-database connection.
  QoS 1 PUBACK means broker acceptance, not database success.
  No durable forwarding queue or offline replay; outages can lose readings.
  After restarting an input broker, explicitly restart its Spin listener.
  Host-side credential/broker helpers remain under pwerusage/deploy.
endlegend
@enduml
